n- **F.** Git-worktree concurrency isolation under a managed, git-ignored location; worktree created on launch, removed on kill; orphan reaper.\n- **G.** Stage handoffs â€” a build launch finds the most-recent plan set and asks \"execute on this plan set?\", pre-staging the worktree.\n- **H.** Runnable Anchor deliverable â€” `anchor_gui.py` Run action spins up a preview on an **OS-assigned ephemeral port** (never the live :8777), bounded and reaped.\n- **I.** Robustness/persistence â€” sessions/PTYs/worktrees/previews run under the `anchor` service, survive RDP disconnect; reaper handles dead sessions, orphan worktrees, stale previews.\n\n### Binding constraints\n- Stdlib-only except the terminal subsystem (declared `pywinpty` exception; distro scan + healthcheck updated to know it).\n- **No live `claude`/`gemini` in the test gate** â€” exercised via `tests/fake_claude.py` (`ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`) + stub PTY backend; ConPTY-under-service proof is a separate manual/orchestrator check.\n- `anchor_gui.py` HTML is f-string-generated (doubled braces); `_PROJECT_WINDOW_JS` is a raw single-brace string.\n- Terminal/preview/worktree endpoints token-authed; GET endpoints stay read-only/unauthenticated. Mirror new data functions into `anchor.py`. Runtime otherwise unchanged (NSSM `anchor`, localhost:8777, single-instance guard).\n\n### Out of scope (Grass Catchers)\n- General multi-user/multi-tenant terminal server; cross-machine sync of `.anchor`/worktrees; auto-merging worktree results without user review.\n\n> **Outcome (per CLAUDE.md / Execution Log):** this plan was subsequently BUILT by Foreman (all 10 waves GREEN, 529 passed) and merged to master 2026-06-12 (commit `208bce1`).\n\nAll claims above are grounded in `planning/rnd-v3/MASTER-PLAN.md`; the build-outcome line is grounded in the project's CLAUDE.md and the Execution Log member doc."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":638,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4176,"cache_r